    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d616">

                <pb facs="0591" n="579" sameAs="frus:frus1940v01/pg579"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">761.62/795: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Germany</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Morris</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Secretary of State
                    </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berlin</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-11-13T17:00:00+02:00">November 13,
                            1940—5 p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 11:50 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>4700. My 4684, November 12, 6 p.m.<anchor n="51" xml:id="d616-f1"/> Molotov was
                    the guest of honor at a party given by Ribbentrop last night at the Kaiserhof
                    Hotel for members of the Soviet delegation and Embassy and German officials.
                    Today he was received for a long conversation by Goering and also called upon
                        Hess.<anchor n="52" xml:id="d616-f2"/> He is scheduled to depart for Moscow
                    tomorrow morning.</p>
                <p>According to a German official the party was a great success and Molotov who
                    speaks some German made an excellent impression on <pb facs="0592" n="580"
                        xml:id="pg580"/> the Germans. The source said that all of the Russians gave
                    evidence of being sincerely pleased and satisfied with current developments in
                    Russo-German relations. He remarked that announcements of startling agreements
                    or new treaties should not be expected, and added this is only the
                    beginning.</p>
                <p>Repeated to Moscow.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Morris</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d616-f1" n="51" xml:id="d616-f1-content">
                <p>Not printed.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d616-f2" n="52" xml:id="d616-f2-content">
                <p>Rudolf Hess, member of the German Reichstag, Minister without Portfolio; Chairman
                    of the Central Committee of the Nazi Party.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
